<p>In 30 years, Panini stickers have shrunk in size by almost <code>14%</code>. The reasoning behind this is due to the massive team size of the World Cup, having so many stickers would otherwise cause the sticker book to weigh as much as a heavy textbook. So this &ldquo;shrinkflation&rdquo; effect is disguised as a way to protect our children&rsquo;s backs. Clever.</p>
<p>
